  "schematicNotes": [
    {
      "id": "n_can",
      "text": "CAN BUS harness. 1 Mbit/s ISO 11898-2. Every CAN node uses 55PC1243-20-2/6/4/5-9 (cab_sh_4c), one common braid around all four wires (Daniel 2026-10-01: the single-shield cable is fine). Cluster, RealDash, CSB3, lambda and the trunk carry +12V, ground, CAN H and CAN L on that cable. Power and ground splice with the CAN pairs at sp_can12 / sp_cang / sp_canh / sp_canl. At the ECU they split: +12V and ground break off to ST185-A-cabin sp_sw12 (F9 / a5) and sp_chassis (a25 / a34) so CAN nodes are powered when the ECU is; the Link CANLTW pigtail red and black land on those same rails. CAN H and CAN L continue as labeled wires that mate to the Link CANLTW round plug (not drawn; do not invent it). Daniel's pin-5 shield pass-through is on a different 6-pin DTM that is also not drawn; do not invent that connector. ecu_com is the six-pin comms / tuning port. Do not land the CAN braid on any of its cavities (c5 is RS232 TX even when unused). The braid joins at sp_can_sh and ends at the ground symbol t_can_sh_gnd with no pin number. Do not land a CAN screen on ecu_com, A7, B17, sp_shield_a or sp_shield_b. Device ends of the screens stay floating, including the lambda controller. Lambda shield has no bulkhead pin. Cluster and RealDash have no node connector on this drawing; their 12V / ground are flying-lead terminals, not invented cavities. 120R termination at the ECU-end splices and at the lambda end. Raychem S200-3-WI-22-9 only on the terminated screen join at sp_can_sh.",
      "width": 390,
      "schematicPosition": {
        "x": 3180,
        "y": 0
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "n_cavity_notes",
      "text": "CAVITY NOTES - full text of the signals marked * on this drawing\nLink CAN-Lambda c1: Power +12V ign, cabin fuse F5 10A - on the 4-core with CAN H/L, continues on ST185-B-engine, bulkhead B c3, ST185-B-cabin, from ST185-CabinPower fuse F5\nt_cluster_can / t_cluster_12v / t_cluster_gnd: TrackCluster ESP32-P4 - CAN drop (device not in this harness; no connector cavities here)\nt_realdash_can / t_realdash_12v / t_realdash_gnd: RealDash Pi 5 - CAN drop (device not in this harness; no connector cavities here)\nt_ltw_h / t_ltw_l: Link CANLTW round plug not drawn; labeled wires that mate to it. Do not invent the plug.\nbr_w_csb12 / br_w_csbg: ECU switched +12V (sp_sw12) and ECU ground (sp_chassis) on ST185-A-cabin; Link CANLTW pigtail red/black land on the same rails. Not ecu_com.\nt_can_sh_gnd: CAN braid ground symbol, no pin number. Not ecu_com, not A7, not B17.",
      "schematicPosition": {
        "x": 3180,
        "y": 150
      }
    }
  ],
